<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh June oil output falls 4.5 pct to 2.16 mln T.</title>
<headline>Kazakh June oil output falls 4.5 pct to 2.16 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan's production of crude oil and gas condensate fell to 2.16 million tonnes in June from 2.26 million tonnes in May, the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>The committee provided the following figures:</p>
<p>  KAZAKH ENERGY OUTPUT	 JUNE 97	MAY 97     JAN-JUNE 97</p>
<p>  CRUDE OIL (million tonnes)  2.161	 2.263	  12.707</p>
<p>   mth/mth pct change	  -4.5	  +6.1	     n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr pct change	   +18.9	 +18.9	   +16.1</p>
<p>NATURAL GAS</p>
<p>   (billion cubic metres)     0.791	 0.496	   4.131</p>
<p>   mth/mth pct change	 +59.3	 -24.3	     n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr pct change	   +78.3	  +1.7	   +30.5</p>
<p>  GASOLINE (tonnes)	   149,000     126,100	 823,500</p>
<p>   mth/mth pct change	 +18.2	 -37.6	     n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr pct change	   -19.5	 -33.9	   -31.3</p>
<p>  DIESEL (tonnes)	     224,500    309,500	1,374,900</p>
<p>   mth/mth pct change	 -27.5	+23.0		n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr pct change	   -27.1	 +4.9	    -14.6</p>
<p>  FUEL OIL (tonnes)	   224,700    230,300	1,644,200</p>
<p>   mth/mth pct change	  -2.4	-13.2		n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr pct change	   -24.7	-19.5	    -12.9</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, + 7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
